  "conversionNotes": [
    "The Ostermark PDF contains NO roster, profiles, costs or equipment lists: it says Ostermarkers 'follow the rules for Mercenary warbands as given on page 48 of the Mordheim rulebook'. Roster, profiles, limits and lists were taken from Mercenaries.pdf (Reikland Mercenaries text, no city rules applied) and checked against its page images. A human should confirm this is the intended reading.",
    "Skill tables use the Reikland Mercenary table (Captain all five; Champion Combat, Shooting, Strength; Youngblood Combat, Speed) since p.48 is the Reikland entry; Reikland Archery Tradition (+1 BS Marksmen) and Military Discipline (12\") are NOT applied.",
    "Wardog is described only as a free starting option for the Captain (rulebook p.54 profile not in this PDF); recorded as fixedEquipment text.",
    "No d6 'roll of X' wording in the warband rules; the all-alone re-roll needs no conversion. Scenario content (Eerie Downs, Battle for the Farm, wyrdstone note) is out of scope.",
    "Starting experience (Captain 20, Champion 8, Youngblood 0, henchmen 0) follows the Mercenary base entry as used in reikland.json; not printed in the Ostermark PDF."
  ]
